---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const snapshot = [
  { label: "Client / Program", value: "Prudential" },
  { label: "Role", value: "Sr. UX/UI Consultant" },
  { label: "Product", value: "Web / Responsive" },
  { label: "Industry", value: "Financial Services / Insurance" },
];

const methodology = [
  "Frame - Align and define",
  "Discover - Research and empathize",
  "Structure - Information architecture",
  "Ideate - Explore concepts",
  "Interact - Optimize flows",
  "Design - Visual and systems",
  "Validate - Test and reduce risk",
  "Launch - Build and QA",
  "Improve - Measure and learn",
];

const deliverables = [
  "Modern life-term policy purchasing journey",
  "Small business insurance product offering flows",
  "Interactive calculators and projection models",
  "Comparison tools for policy evaluation",
  "Educational content and guidance",
  "Fully responsive website design",
  "Self-service decision-support tools",
];

const methods = [
  "Sketch",
  "InVision",
  "Axure RP",
  "Responsive web design",
  "Wireframing",
  "Interactive prototyping",
  "Usability testing",
  "A/B testing",
];

const outcomes = [
  "Supported clearer user decision-making around insurance products",
  "Reduced friction in self-service exploration and comparison flows",
  "Improved comprehension of complex insurance offerings",
  "Helped reduce dependence on assisted support through clearer digital guidance",
  "Strengthened responsive access across devices",
  "Created a more guided insurance purchasing and evaluation journey",
];

const workedWell = [
  "Interactive tools helped users visualize and evaluate insurance needs.",
  "Responsive design improved access across devices.",
  "Simplifying complex insurance jargon into user-friendly language improved comprehension.",
];

const improvements = [
  "Stronger personalization features could have tailored recommendations more directly to individual user profiles.",
  "Additional tutorial resources or guided videos could have further supported users through the decision-making process.",
];

const takeaways = [
  "User empowerment depends on clarity, guidance, and confidence.",
  "Iterative testing and user feedback are essential when simplifying complex financial products.",
  "Clear educational resources can reduce product complexity and improve self-service experiences.",
];
---

<MainLayout
  title="Life Insurance Digital Experience | Jorge Obando"
  description="Prudential case study by Jorge Obando, covering life insurance experience design, responsive web design, self-service decision support, calculators, comparison tools, and educational content."
  ogImage="/images/prudential-life-insurance-digital-experience-case-study.png"
>
  <section class="case-study-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Prudential</p>
        <h1>Life Insurance Digital Experience</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          A responsive digital experience designed to simplify life insurance
          decision-making through clearer guidance, self-service tools, interactive
          calculators, comparison flows, and educational content.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="hero-image">
        <img
          src="/images/prudential-life-insurance-digital-experience-case-study.png"
          alt="Prudential life insurance digital experience interface screenshot"
        />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="snapshot-grid" aria-label="Case study snapshot">
      {snapshot.map((item) => (
        <article class="snapshot-card">
          <p class="snapshot-label">{item.label}</p>
          <p class="snapshot-value">{item.value}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Prudential faced a common challenge in the life insurance space: consumers
        often found insurance products complex, jargon-heavy, and difficult to
        compare.
      </p>
      <p>
        As Sr. UX/UI Consultant, Jorge supported the redesign of a digital experience
        focused on helping users better understand their options, navigate life
        insurance and small business insurance offerings, and use self-service tools
        to make more confident decisions.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work included responsive web design, educational content, interactive
        calculators, projection models, comparison tools, and decision-support flows
        intended to reduce friction in the insurance exploration and purchasing
        journey.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prudential needed to improve the clarity and usability of its digital
        experience so consumers could better understand insurance options, compare
        products, and make more informed decisions with less dependence on assisted
        support.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>The real problem</h2>
      <p>
        The life insurance industry has long been perceived as complex and daunting,
        especially for consumers making high-stakes decisions about their financial
        futures.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prudential faced a significant business challenge: users were struggling with
        clarity and confidence when navigating life insurance and small business
        insurance options.
      </p>
      <p>
        This created increased dependence on call centers and assisted support,
        revealing a gap in digital self-service capabilities.
      </p>
      <p>
        The mission was to transform the digital experience so users could better
        understand product options, evaluate tradeoffs, and move through the
        decision-making process with greater independence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Role and leadership</h2>
      <p>
        As Sr. UX/UI Consultant, Jorge supported a multidisciplinary team responsible
        for redefining Prudential's digital life insurance experience.
      </p>
      <p>
        His role included visual design, interaction design, user-centered design
        strategy, stakeholder collaboration, and coordination with product managers,
        developers, and business stakeholders.
      </p>
      <p>
        He helped translate complex insurance concepts into clearer digital flows,
        supported self-service decision-making, and ensured that design solutions
        aligned with both business strategy and customer needs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        The work followed a research-led, structure-first design process with
        continuous validation. The approach emphasized research over opinion,
        structure before surface, and continuous usability validation.
      </p>
      <div class="cards-grid three-up">
        {methodology.map((item) => (
          <article class="info-card compact-card">
            <p>{item}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Key deliverables</h2>
      <div class="outcomes-card">
        <ul>
          {deliverables.map((item) => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Design process</h2>
      <div class="cards-grid one-up">
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Research and discovery</h3>
          <p>
            The team used a mixed-methods research approach to understand user
            challenges and preferences.
          </p>
          <p>
            Research activities included user interviews, usability testing of current
            digital offerings, and competitor analysis.
          </p>
          <p>
            Key insights showed that users often felt lost in the insurance purchasing
            journey, citing confusion around jargon, unclear product differences, and
            a lack of straightforward guidance.
          </p>
          <p>
            By synthesizing qualitative feedback with available analytics, the team
            identified pain points that informed design strategies and reinforced the
            need for clearer educational content and decision support.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Information architecture</h3>
          <p>
            The information architecture strategy focused on simplifying the insurance
            journey through clearer categorization, user-friendly language, and
            navigational paths aligned with user expectations.
          </p>
          <p>
            The team prioritized plain language over jargon, introduced educational
            resource structures, and organized content to support easier comparison
            and decision-making.
          </p>
          <p>
            This structure helped demystify insurance products and gave users clearer
            pathways through complex product information.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Prototyping and testing</h3>
          <p>
            Prototyping was central to the methodology, ranging from low-fidelity
            wireframes to high-fidelity clickable prototypes.
          </p>
          <p>
            The team conducted usability testing with target users to gather feedback
            on comprehension, navigation, and interaction patterns.
          </p>
          <p>
            A/B testing methods were also used to validate design decisions against
            user preferences and refine the experience through iteration.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Iterations and refinements</h3>
          <p>
            The design process went through multiple iterations informed by user
            feedback.
          </p>
          <p>
            Initial prototypes highlighted issues around navigation clarity, content
            overload, and decision-making friction.
          </p>
          <p>
            Subsequent versions streamlined interactions, prioritized essential
            information, and introduced interactive calculators and comparison tools
            that gave users more control over the evaluation process.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Technologies and methods</h2>
      <div class="tag-list" aria-label="Technologies and methods">
        {methods.map((item) => (
          <span>{item}</span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Outcomes</h2>
      <p>
        The design work supported Prudential's goals around improving digital
        self-service, making complex insurance products easier to understand, and
        reducing friction in the insurance decision-making process.
      </p>
      <p>
        By introducing clearer educational content, responsive journeys, interactive
        calculators, comparison tools, and decision-support flows, the experience
        helped users evaluate options with greater confidence and reduced reliance on
        assisted support.
      </p>
      <div class="outcomes-card">
        <ul>
          {outcomes.map((item) => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Reflection</h2>
      <div class="cards-grid one-up">
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>What worked well</h3>
          <ul>
            {workedWell.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Areas for improvement</h3>
          <ul>
            {improvements.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
          <ul>
            {takeaways.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Why this matters</h2>
      <p>
        Insurance experiences require clarity, trust, plain language, and guided
        self-service because users are making complex, high-stakes financial
        decisions. Strong digital guidance helps people understand options, compare
        tradeoffs, and move forward with greater confidence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Related Thinking</h2>
      <section class="article-links" aria-label="Related thinking and next navigation">
        <a href="/thinking/measuring-what-matters">
          Why measuring outcomes - not outputs - changes execution
        </a>
        <a href="/thinking/designing-through-change">
          Designing systems that evolve through change
        </a>
        <a href="/case-studies">
          Return to all case studies
        </a>
      </section>
    </section>
  </section>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .case-study-page {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(320px, 0.9fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .hero-copy {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #a33a3a;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw, 4.15rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .lead {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #555;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .hero-image {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--divider);
    border-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .hero-image img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 280px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .snapshot-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .snapshot-card,
  .info-card,
  .outcomes-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--divider);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .snapshot-card {
    padding: 1.2rem;
  }

  .snapshot-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #777;
  }

  .snapshot-value {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #222;
  }

  .content-section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 2.2vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .content-section p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #444;
    line-height: 1.8;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .cards-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .cards-grid.three-up {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .cards-grid.one-up {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .info-card {
    padding: 1.4rem;
  }

  .compact-card {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .info-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .info-card p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .info-card p:last-child,
  .compact-card p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .info-card ul,
  .outcomes-card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .info-card li,
  .outcomes-card li {
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #444;
  }

  .info-card li:last-child,
  .outcomes-card li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .outcomes-card {
    padding: 1.35rem 1.4rem;
  }

  .tag-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .tag-list span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--divider);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    color: #444;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .article-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .article-links a {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .snapshot-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .cards-grid.three-up {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .case-study-page {
      padding: 1.5rem 0 4rem;
    }

    .snapshot-grid,
    .cards-grid.three-up {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.02rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .hero-image img {
      min-height: 220px;
    }

    .article-links {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }
  }
</style>
